From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:47:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 66/86] Images inside headings, lists and tables render inline
 in the preview

The Markdown widget draws an image in a heading, a list item or a table
cell as a block of its own and loses the text before it. A heading, list
or table that holds an image is now drawn by the HTML pass: headings as
an inline heading row, list items parsed again as documents of their own
(numbers, task boxes and nested lists kept), table cells as inline rows
with the column alignment. Images scale down to fit, as in paragraphs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

